    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Bug Fixed! \n\nThe issue was **floating-point precision** when converting prices to cents. When you typed `39.95`, the code was multiplying it by 100, which JavaScript represented as `3995.0000000000005` instead of exactly `3995` \u2014 failing the integer check.\n\n**Root cause:** In three functions, prices were converted via floating-point arithmetic:\n- `parseEuros()` in `src/money.js`\n- `decimalCommaToCents()` in `src/locale.js`  \n- `cellCents()` in `src/money.js`\n\n**The fix:** Instead of multiplying floating-point numbers, I extract the euro and cent parts as strings, then concatenate them to form an integer directly. For example, `\"39.95\"` becomes `3995` without any floating-point math.\n\n\u2705 All 50 tests pass  \n\u2705 Your gym membership (39.95) now adds successfully  \n\u2705 Other prices (12.99, 10.99) continue to work  \n\u2705 Previously problematic prices (9.95, 29.95, 49.95) are now fixed too",
